WEBVTT

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:15.330
Hey.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:36.010
The Faraway Paladin

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:39.870
Where do you think you're going?

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:42.710
Where?

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.430
To kill the demon beasts.

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:49.700
Alone?

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:51.320
Yeah.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.800
I doubt you can keep up with me.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.990
<i>Which is why I need to protect him.</i>

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.880
Don't worry. It'll be okay.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.910
I'll take care of everything.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.130
I'll kill the chimera and the 
whole herd of demon beasts.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:14.150
If there are demons controlling 
them, I'll kill them, too.

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:18.300
That's just the kind of 
monster I am, apparently.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:21.540
You...

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:25.740
Stop screwing around!

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:27.530
Wake the hell up!

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:28.990
You idiot!

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:34.720
<i>Oh, so this is how it has to be.</i>

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:38.090
Is that all, Meneldor?

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:48.310
Damn it!

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.830
<i>I can't have him following me.</i>

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:00.520
Damn it!

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:04.690
Damn it!

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:07.510
Damn it!

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:09.000
Damn it!

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:13.700
<i>I guess I could break just one arm.</i>

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:28.750
Get someone to heal you.

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:32.030
I'm...

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:34.070
I'm not done!

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:38.210
Oh? You're more resilient than I thought.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:40.560
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:43.450
<i>Use Words to hold him in place?</i>

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:46.110
<i>No, I'll constrict his carotids 
so he loses consci—</i>

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:48.420
Gnomes, O gnomes, clench your fists!

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:50.680
Use them to strike the enemy!

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:52.620
Useless incantation.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:57.360
<i>No! If I dodge it, the magic will hit Menel!</i>

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:08.150
What's this crap about 
fixing everything alone?

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.790
You're just being a coward!

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.260
Did you really have to go that far?

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:21.010
What?

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:23.480
We were only together because 
things worked out that way.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:26.460
There was no reason for you to do that.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:28.940
Yeah, that's true.

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:31.820
I have no reason to go out of my way

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:35.110
to stop an emotionally unstable 
coward who's completely lost it

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:37.120
just because he got his 
ass handed to him once.

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:38.650
Then—

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:39.410
But...

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:41.400
You're my friend.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.850
And friends stick together.

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:47.740
If my friend goes nuts, 
I want to do something for him.

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:51.080
Menel...

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:54.310
You don't know much about your own origins,

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:56.440
and you're clueless about the world.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:58.840
There've been times when I 
thought you seemed suspicious.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.530
But you're a nice guy.

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:05.310
I know you're trying to do things right, 
and doing your best at everything.

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:11.570
You saved my life, you saved that village...

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:15.370
We traveled together, we fought together...

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:17.890
And I enjoyed spending time with you.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:22.260
I'm grateful to you from the bottom of my 
heart for sending off those villagers.

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:27.870
Will, you are my friend, 
and I don't abandon my friends.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:36.480
Well, you still wanna fight?

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.820
I surrender.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:44.860
I'm still weaker than you now,

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:46.300
but just wait.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.620
I'll catch up before you know it.

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:50.510
Menel...

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:52.990
I'll prove to you soon enough

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:54.530
that you're no monster.

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:02.380
Okay.

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:06.050
I'll wait. I'll be waiting for you.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:09.650
Man, you're a real pain in the ass!

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:14.530
Sorry. I kinda lost control of myself.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.540
Well, it happens—ow!

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:18.630
I'll heal that—

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.290
But a surrender's a surrender.

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:22.630
That means I win!

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:26.610
I only surrendered because 
you wouldn't give it a rest!

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:27.580
Keep whining!

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:30.590
Wow...

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:36.940
<i>And so we kept exchanging 
dumb jokes and laughter.</i>

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:36.250
What a pretty sight. The moon's 
congratulating me on my victory.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:39.190
What? Want me to break your other arm?

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:40.630
<i>It was my first ever argument with a friend,</i>

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:43.960
<i>and I guess I lost.</i>

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:48.850
Oh, you're back, eh?

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:48.350
Welcome back!

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:51.490
Will! Menel!

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:53.070
Welcome back!

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:54.790
You jerks! You had me worried!

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:57.080
Sorry, Bee.

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:58.510
Will...

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:02.700
If you don't mind, would you 
please tell me what happened?

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:08.000
Sure.

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:16.010
That's an illness of the strong.

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:19.680
The stronger you are, 
the harder it hits you.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:22.900
Depending on the case, it can even kill you.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:26.470
I'm really sorry for 
making all of you worry.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.960
But I'm all right now.

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:38.990
You were just stuck in bed not long ago,

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:40.620
and you were off slugging it out?

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:42.660
We even set a trap for a surprise attack.

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:44.490
That chimera's got no chance!

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:46.660
You said it!

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:49.650
I've got a debt to repay to that bastard.

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:51.620
I won't be humiliated like that again.

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:55.210
You're gonna fight that thing again?

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:57.860
Yeah. We're going for a return match.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:00.030
I refuse to just get beat 
up and leave it at that.

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:03.150
I'll split all three of that 
demon beast's heads open.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:09.410
Chimeras don't occur naturally.

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:12.780
That thing is, without a doubt, 
the product of a demonic ritual.

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:15.540
Let's take all of them out at once, 
before they can escape.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:18.970
So soon after it roughed us up that bad?

00:07:18.970 --> 00:07:20.760
I can't just give up and leave it like this.

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:22.030
Let's bust 'em up good!

00:07:22.030 --> 00:07:24.810
All right, guess we should 
round up some help, huh?

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:28.030
It's gonna be a good, fun, 
stupid-as-hell adventure!

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:30.210
You'll get one silver coin 
for a demon beast's head,

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:33.170
and ten gold coins for the demon boss's!

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:51.960
<i>After that, we spent a few days 
getting a force together,</i>

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:54.790
<i>sent out several rounds of scouts, 
and made our preparations.</i>

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:57.180
<i>We didn't arrange any special tricks.</i>

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:01.560
<i>We'd just get enough people together, 
make preparations ahead,</i>

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:03.610
<i>and face our enemy head-on.</i>

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:15.310
Let's set up our formation and gear here.

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:19.820
Anna and the other priests, 
please support us from here.

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:20.940
Right!

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:24.470
When we're all ready, we'll send 
our front line to the battle zone!

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:34.540
If we can wipe out all of those,

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:36.980
this whole area's gonna be 
a whole lot more peaceful.

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:38.580
Yeah.

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:39.910
Let's wipe them out.

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:43.320
Sometimes you say the wildest 
things so casually.

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:44.300
Here they come.

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:53.810
I'll back you up.

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:56.240
Okay. I'm counting on you, Menel.

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:58.730
We'll break through head-on!

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:05.430
By Volt's blade of lightning!

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:08.140
Burn bright, Blaze's flames of courage!

00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:12.400
Whirl, send us a tailwind of good fortune!

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:14.350
Grant us the divine protection 
of all the virtuous gods!

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:19.550
Shoot!

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:22.510
Sagitta Flammeum!

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:22.290
Flame Arrow

00:09:28.030 --> 00:09:29.170
<i>It's war!</i>

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:33.240
Stand ready!

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:39.800
Goddess of flux, repel the 
poisons that rain down upon us!

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:40.880
Fortis...

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:40.850
Strong

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:41.800
Vita!

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:41.600
Life

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:09.650
<i>How could I say I'd fix all this alone?</i>

00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:12.840
<i>I was never any more than 
one factor in this battle.</i>

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:14.850
<i>The battlefield isn't so easy</i>

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:17.460
<i>that just one dose of penetrating 
strength is enough!</i>

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:22.470
By the flame of Gracefeel!

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:28.730
According to reports,

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:32.640
the campaign to eliminate the demon 
beasts should be starting by now.

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:36.770
I wonder, will these great Wyvern Killers

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:40.610
succeed in a new heroic feat 
for the bards to sing about?

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:41.740
Hmph.

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:46.560
The temple has bent over backwards 
to facilitate that novice boy.

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:49.240
If he fails to succeed in this,

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:51.530
he will not be worthy of our backing.

00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:53.580
By the way, Bishop,

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:55.770
I hear you entrusted your daughter, Anna,

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:59.950
and many other brilliant 
priests to the paladin.

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:04.080
Losing valuable talent to the philanthropic 
exploits of such a novice

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:06.270
has caused nothing but trouble for me!

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:12.400
What's this?

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:14.930
The abandoned remains of a monastery?

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:18.000
Looks like we're the first ones here.

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:20.640
Be careful. There might be traps.

00:11:34.150 --> 00:11:35.010
Omnia...

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:34.840
Everything

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:35.990
Vanitas.

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:35.840
In Vain

00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:37.280
Erasus.

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:37.090
Erasure

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:44.900
Hi there.

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:47.190
It was waiting in ambush with Invisibility?

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:50.740
Careful, Will. 
This thing's pretty damn smart.

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:54.200
Do you think maybe it's 
got some demon in it?

00:11:57.290 --> 00:11:59.660
Are you after the High King?

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:01.140
Oh?

00:12:01.140 --> 00:12:03.610
You know the High King's seal.

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:07.000
Are you a warrior sent by one of the gods?

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:09.890
<i>That answer... I'm certain now.</i>

00:12:11.900 --> 00:12:15.050
<i>Basically, this is like taking 
a square on a chess board.</i>

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:17.860
<i>The city of the dead, where 
the High King was sealed,</i>

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:20.650
<i>isn't yet under either side's control.</i>

00:12:21.410 --> 00:12:25.260
<i>If the demons take control, 
they'll undo the seal,</i>

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:27.550
<i>and disaster will ravage 
the continent again.</i>

00:12:28.090 --> 00:12:29.810
<i>But if the people take control,</i>

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:31.740
<i>the seal will likely become even stronger.</i>

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:34.650
<i>The demons are in a position</i>

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:37.620
<i>where they need to keep Beast Woods 
permanently devastated.</i>

00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:41.190
<i>They need to keep it in a state of 
chaos, destitution, and lawlessness.</i>

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:45.950
<i>That's why they're commanding demon beasts 
to attack villages and keep the pressure on.</i>

00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:49.210
<i>They can't let mankind 
advance any further south.</i>

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:52.300
<i>They can't let people head toward the south.</i>

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:55.620
<i>They can't let them think 
there's hope in the south.</i>

00:12:57.390 --> 00:12:59.400
<i>If you consider the existence of their king,</i>

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:02.960
<i>it's incredibly easy to figure 
out what their objective is.</i>

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:08.940
In the name of the goddess of flux, 
I will destroy all of you.

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:12.370
Oh? But wait.

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:16.660
There seems to be some sort of mistake, 
or perhaps a misunderstanding.

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:19.090
A misunderstanding, you say?

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:20.450
Yes.

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:23.100
In truth...

00:13:31.770 --> 00:13:35.740
Demons like to stick to the classics 
in their surprise attacks, don't they?

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:39.010
Menel!

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:39.850
Yep!

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:42.080
Sagitta Flammeum!

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:41.960
Flame Arrow

00:13:42.390 --> 00:13:43.740
I'm not takin' that hit!

00:13:43.740 --> 00:13:45.880
Sylphs, sylphs, maidens of wind!

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:50.640
Gracefeel, grant us your protection!

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:54.260
<i>Don't stop it!</i>

00:13:54.260 --> 00:13:55.130
<i>Divert it!</i>

00:13:58.130 --> 00:14:00.160
Gnomes, O gnomes, slip underfoot!

00:14:00.160 --> 00:14:02.320
Tighten, bind, and tie it down!

00:14:13.610 --> 00:14:15.180
<i>It has multiple heads.</i>

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:17.460
<i>If each one takes a different 
reflexive action,</i>

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:19.380
<i>they're sure to end up confused.</i>

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:22.540
<i>This demon beast is unnatural 
in terms of living beings!</i>

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:28.090
<i>I don't need to score a clean 
victory in one strike.</i>

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:31.070
<i>I just need to fight it the right 
way and win by being better.</i>

00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:33.840
<i>I don't need a flashy secret technique.</i>

00:14:33.840 --> 00:14:35.810
<i>I'll just use all three of their teachings</i>

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:37.510
<i>and do what it takes to win!</i>

00:14:38.540 --> 00:14:41.730
<i>That's the fighting style 
that's best for me!</i>

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:45.910
Maidens of wind, 
bless this arrow with your kiss!

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:57.250
That's one down!

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:07.000
Although I detest this dragon power, 
you leave me with no choice!

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:08.150
<i>Dragon?</i>

00:15:11.810 --> 00:15:12.920
This one, too?

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:13.730
Menel.

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:16.070
Get back a little farther.

00:15:16.070 --> 00:15:17.660
I'll strike it down now.

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:20.090
<i>I was raised on Mary's bread,</i>

00:15:20.090 --> 00:15:22.300
<i>and my arms bear Mater's stigma,</i>

00:15:23.050 --> 00:15:25.490
<i>so poisons don't work on me.</i>

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:28.990
<i>I'm sure you'd like some 
glory of your own, too, huh?</i>

00:15:40.530 --> 00:15:42.910
Gnomes, O gnomes, clench your fists!

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:45.160
Use them to strike the enemy!

00:15:51.770 --> 00:15:53.810
<i>There's nowhere to run to the left or right!</i>

00:15:53.810 --> 00:15:54.630
<i>Then...</i>

00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:56.650
Acceleratio!

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:56.430
Accelerate

00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:03.680
Gnomes, O gnomes, slip underfoot!

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:05.640
Tighten, bind, and tie it down!

00:16:20.740 --> 00:16:21.540
We won!

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:22.400
All right!

00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:30.220
On to the next one.

00:16:30.220 --> 00:16:30.940
Yep.

00:16:41.780 --> 00:16:43.050
Took you long enough.

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:46.250
Reystov?

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:49.060
I'll be taking those ten gold coins.

00:16:49.060 --> 00:16:51.320
What?! He beat us to it?!

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:53.320
You're kidding! How'd you do it?!

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:54.790
Came around from the side.

00:16:55.170 --> 00:16:58.320
Since you guys were taking 
care of the chimera for me,

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:00.050
it was actually pretty easy.

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:03.530
That's Reystov the Penetrator for you.

00:17:03.530 --> 00:17:05.490
He's way too good at getting 
the jump on people.

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:09.350
You have to be, if you want to 
get to the strongest opponents.

00:17:09.350 --> 00:17:12.190
Careful! No telling what 
kinda traps are in here!

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:14.550
Heh, we're the first ones here!

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:16.600
And those ten gold coins are ours!

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:17.110
Huh?

00:17:20.630 --> 00:17:22.450
To our victory!

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:47.230
Episode 12 
The Faraway Paladin

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:51.600
What do you think?

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:54.750
I'm happy, but still kinda embarrassed...

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:56.630
I feel like you embellished a bit too much.

00:18:56.630 --> 00:18:59.870
This kinda thing is supposed 
to be a little embellished!

00:18:59.870 --> 00:19:02.170
Hey, someone who gets it!

00:19:02.170 --> 00:19:05.240
I'll write a song about you next, Menel!

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:05.940
Huh?

00:19:05.940 --> 00:19:09.780
Maybe I'll give you the nickname 
"Meneldor the Beautiful"!

00:19:09.780 --> 00:19:12.970
The one who walks the hero's path 
along with the Faraway Paladin!

00:19:12.970 --> 00:19:16.440
Hey, isn't that gonna make people 
think I'm actually a woman?

00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:18.440
And you can be Will's girlfriend!

00:19:18.440 --> 00:19:19.450
Don't you dare!

00:19:19.450 --> 00:19:20.390
Aw, it's fine!

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:21.500
It is not!

00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:23.920
<i>After his vehement objections, 
Menel's nickname was revised</i>

00:19:23.920 --> 00:19:27.510
<i>from "Meneldor the Beautiful" 
to "Meneldor of Swift Wings."</i>

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:32.880
It's so much more lively now.

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:35.950
And it's gonna get more and 
more lively from now on.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:37.320
I hope so.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:39.590
What're you talking about? 
Of course it will.

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:42.020
The threat of the demons and 
demon beasts has faded.

00:19:42.020 --> 00:19:45.520
People searching for new lands 
are gonna flock to the south.

00:19:45.520 --> 00:19:48.490
There'll probably be problems, 
too, but that's how it goes.

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:50.330
I guess so.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:54.000
Also, I'll say this since you'll 
find out eventually anyway.

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:56.790
The villagers are building a shrine.

00:19:56.790 --> 00:19:58.390
A shrine?

00:19:58.390 --> 00:20:00.230
The one they talked about 
back at the meeting hall.

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:02.920
They made an altar to hold votive candles,

00:20:02.920 --> 00:20:05.420
and they decided to make 
it a shrine to Gracefeel.

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:07.830
To the goddess of light?

00:20:08.550 --> 00:20:12.380
<i>It's the first step toward 
growing her following again!</i>

00:20:12.930 --> 00:20:15.530
By the way, what are you gonna do next?

00:20:15.530 --> 00:20:16.490
Next?

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:19.140
Well, there's still a lot of clean-up to—

00:20:19.140 --> 00:20:20.390
I mean after that.

00:20:20.390 --> 00:20:21.350
After that?

00:20:21.350 --> 00:20:23.440
Gonna be the lord of a domain?

00:20:23.440 --> 00:20:25.680
Huh? A lord? For what domain?

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:27.870
The villages of Beast Woods.

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:28.670
Who is?

00:20:28.670 --> 00:20:29.590
You.

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:33.260
Oh, come on!

00:20:33.260 --> 00:20:37.090
I am a knight, but a 
single-generation one with no land.

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:39.380
I'm no different from an 
adventurer, really...

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:41.510
Is that seriously what you think?

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:42.280
Huh?

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:45.820
For real? You didn't even 
know what you were?

00:20:46.210 --> 00:20:46.970
Huh?

00:20:46.970 --> 00:20:48.940
Just so I'm clear here...

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:51.970
If you wanted to do business in this 
forest, who would you talk to?

00:20:51.970 --> 00:20:53.240
Tonio?

00:20:53.240 --> 00:20:55.780
But didn't most of the funds come from you?

00:20:55.780 --> 00:20:57.230
Well, yeah, but...

00:20:57.230 --> 00:20:58.100
Listen to me!

00:20:58.100 --> 00:21:02.090
First of all, you're a paladin with the 
goddess of light's divine protection

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:04.930
and the approval of both the 
country and the temple.

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:06.310
You have all kinds of power!

00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:09.570
On top of that, you have the military 
authority to gather all these adventurers,

00:21:09.570 --> 00:21:13.370
and by arbitrating for the villages, 
you effectively have jurisdiction over them.

00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:15.460
So, um, you're saying...

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:17.250
In the process of exterminating the demons,

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:19.570
you took control of the flow 
of goods, ruling power,

00:21:19.570 --> 00:21:24.050
military force, jurisdiction, 
and every other kind of authority.

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:27.510
If you say you don't wanna do all that now,

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:29.120
<i>that</i> would be the disaster.

00:21:29.780 --> 00:21:32.560
Are you saying... 
you seriously didn't realize it?

00:21:34.580 --> 00:21:35.810
You...

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:38.960
I just hoped I could do 
something about the demons,

00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:43.530
and improve the impoverished conditions 
in the villages a little bit...

00:21:44.060 --> 00:21:50.320
<i>From there, I just thought I'd make a 
slick exit, like Blood and the other two.</i>

00:21:50.710 --> 00:21:52.780
Um... Menel?

00:21:53.490 --> 00:21:57.130
Wh-What do I do? Should I start 
by getting people together?

00:21:57.130 --> 00:21:59.880
You've already got a merchant 
and priests who know the law.

00:22:00.270 --> 00:22:01.210
If you need more,

00:22:01.210 --> 00:22:03.960
just have the crown prince 
set you up with someone.

00:22:06.110 --> 00:22:09.340
<i>How the heck did I end up in this position?</i>

00:22:09.340 --> 00:22:10.610
<i>Please tell me,</i>

00:22:11.460 --> 00:22:12.790
<i>goddess!</i>

00:22:15.980 --> 00:22:17.020
Then again...

00:22:17.680 --> 00:22:22.350
That does sound like it might 
be a goal worth working toward.

00:22:22.350 --> 00:22:24.870
It's probably gonna be some 
damn hard work, though.

00:22:25.210 --> 00:22:29.050
But as long as I have all of you, 
I'm sure it'll work out.

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:33.840
You'll help me, right?

00:22:36.090 --> 00:22:37.590
Oh, fine.

00:22:38.670 --> 00:22:40.060
I'll stick with you.

00:22:40.330 --> 00:22:43.260
First, we should figure out what 
the demons are plotting...

00:22:43.260 --> 00:22:44.180
Who cares?

00:22:44.180 --> 00:22:46.800
Just grab the bastards and crush 'em 
as soon as you find 'em!

00:22:46.800 --> 00:22:48.160
That's so violent...

00:22:48.160 --> 00:22:51.660
Hey! Will! Menel!

00:22:51.880 --> 00:22:56.220
Stop hiding in your own little 
world and get over here!

00:22:58.350 --> 00:23:02.030
<i>If more people come in and 
everything goes well,</i>

00:23:04.210 --> 00:23:07.320
<i>maybe we'll be able to return to that city.</i>

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:10.920
<i>Maybe we can make the city of the dead</i>

00:23:11.380 --> 00:23:15.840
<i>a regular city where living 
people can laugh together.</i>

00:23:19.180 --> 00:23:23.190
<i>Up on the hill where 
Mary and Blood's graves are,</i>

00:23:23.190 --> 00:23:25.380
<i>the laughter of children will resound,</i>

00:23:25.380 --> 00:23:28.150
<i>and the sounds of people working 
to make a living will return.</i>

00:23:32.220 --> 00:23:36.650
<i>Somehow, that seemed like 
such a wonderful thing to me.</i>
